# Configuration options:
#
# rate_limit_per_minute (optional, default: 100)
#   Maximum API requests per IP per minute.
#
# app_host (optional)
#   Public hostname used in dashboard integration snippets.
#   Example: https://analytics.example.com
#
# brand_name (optional, default: Aggregate Analytics)
#   Application name used in page titles, headings, and explanatory copy.
#
# brand_logo_text (optional, default: brand_name)
#   Text shown beside the optional logo image in application navigation.
#   With a valid image, use an empty value for an image-only identity.
#
# brand_logo_path (optional, default: "")
#   PNG, JPEG, or WebP logo image, at most 2 MiB, 4096 pixels per axis,
#   and 16 megapixels in total.
#   Remove embedded metadata before use; the image bytes are served as supplied.
#   Use an absolute path or a path relative to the project root. An empty value
#   displays only brand_logo_text. UI uploads are copied below var/branding,
#   which must be persisted across deployments and writable by the PHP process.
#
# brand_primary_color (optional, default: "#00D1B2")
#   Primary interactive and emphasis color.
#
# brand_accent_color (optional, default: "#485FC7")
#   Secondary accent color.
#
# brand_navbar_color (optional, default: "#14161A")
#   Navigation bar background color.
#
# brand_background_color (optional, default: "#F5F5F5")
#   Application page background color.
#
# brand_surface_color (optional, default: "#FFFFFF")
#   Cards, panels, and other raised surface color.
#
# brand_text_color (optional, default: "#363636")
#   Main application text color.
#
#   Theme colors accept #RGB or #RRGGBB hexadecimal notation and are normalized
#   to six-digit form. Quote hex colors so YAML does not treat # as a comment.
#   Text must have at least 4.5:1 contrast against both background and surface;
#   lower-contrast YAML/env palettes fall back to safe defaults.
#
# brand_font_family (optional, default: system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, Segoe UI, sans-serif)
#   Safe comma-separated local/system font stack used for application text.
#   Fonts are never downloaded by this setting.
#
# brand_heading_font_family (optional, default: system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, Segoe UI, sans-serif)
#   Safe comma-separated local/system font stack used for headings.
#   Fonts are never downloaded by this setting.
#
# js_namespace (optional, default: Aggregate)
#   JavaScript global variable name: window.{js_namespace}
#   Examples: Aggregate, MyAnalytics, Tracker
#
# dashboard_enabled (optional, default: true)
#   Enable dashboard/install/login UI routes.
#   Set to false for API-only headless deployments managed via CLI/YAML.
#
# internal_traffic_storage (optional, default: cookie)
#   cookie or local_storage. Matching markers add a boolean under the configured
#   name to each raw event's custom_data JSON (default: orgInternalTraffic: true).
#   Grouped BI/archive views omit this flag. No migration is needed.
#
# internal_traffic_name / internal_traffic_value (defaults: orgInternalTraffic / 'true')
#   Shared marker name and value. The admin UI can save these settings and mark
#   the current browser. Names use 1–128 letters, digits, underscores or hyphens;
#   numeric keys and Aggregate identifier names are reserved. The JSON property
#   name matches this browser marker name; historical rows keep their old key
#   after a rename. Values are non-empty strings up to
#   256 bytes; quote YAML values. Uppercase environment variables take precedence.
#
# internal_traffic_cookie_domain (optional, default: '')
#   Empty means this hostname. example.com covers its subdomains; ignored for
#   local storage, which applies only to its exact origin. Cookies last up to one
#   year. Unrelated domains must host the downloaded HTML marker page themselves.
#
# internal_traffic_share_token (optional, default: '')
#   Initial installation generates a random token and persists it to YAML.
#   Empty disables /internal-traffic/{token}. The page also works in headless mode.
#   Generate/rotate/revoke via the admin UI, or generate: openssl rand -hex 32
#   Manual tokens must contain 32–128 URL-safe letters, digits, underscores or hyphens.
#   The page has noindex/nofollow/no-store headers. Share tokens are never included
#   in aggregate.js or downloaded HTML pages. Revocation does not remove markers
#   already applied or downloaded pages hosted elsewhere.
#
# collection_profile (optional, default: standard)
#   standard or strict. Strict records every event in anonymous mode with only
#   the sanitized page path, event name and an approved goal. The served tracker
#   then reads no screen size, referrer or query string and does not read, write
#   or remove cookies or browser storage; the server discards other submitted
#   dimensions and skips geography. Other settings stay saved but unused.
#   Unrecognized values stop ingestion. This limits device access; it does not
#   by itself make collection consent-exempt. See docs/PRIVACY-COMPLIANCE.md.
#
# anonymous_tracking_enabled (optional, default: true)
#   Administrative collection kill switch. Set to false to reject both anonymous
#   and consented enhanced events at the ingestion boundary.
#
# anonymous_excluded_paths (optional, default: [])
#   Paths that must never be collected in either mode. Supports glob patterns
#   such as /account/*, /checkout/**, and /health.
#
# anonymous_geo_enabled (optional, default: false)
#   Derive a coarse area from the request IP for accepted analytics events. Requires
#   a local GeoLite2-Country-compatible MMDB. The IP and detailed lookup record
#   are not added to the event or queue. A lookup failure produces no geo area
#   and does not reject the event.
#
# anonymous_geo_level (optional, default: macro_region)
#   Stored granularity: macro_region or country. Macro-region stores only the
#   MMDB continent code. City, subdivision, postcode, and coordinates are never
#   retained.
#
# anonymous_geo_database_path (optional, default: "")
#   Local GeoLite2-Country-compatible .mmdb file. Use an absolute path
#   (recommended) or a path contained by the project root. Mount it read-only
#   and make it readable by the ingestion process. URI schemes and relative
#   project-root escapes are rejected, as are UNC/network-share and Windows
#   device paths. The app never downloads or sends lookups to a GeoIP service.
#
# analytics_archiving_enabled (optional, default: false)
#   Aggregate eligible raw events into private hourly event/pageview, daily
#   goal, and daily geography cells. Archiving does not itself delete raw rows.
#
# analytics_archive_after_days (optional, default: 90; range: 1..36500)
#   Archive completed raw data older than this many days.
#
# analytics_retention_enabled (optional, default: false)
#   Irreversibly delete raw rows and archived cells after the periods below.
#   Dry-run and verify backups/reporting before enabling this setting.
#
# analytics_anonymous_retention_days (optional, default: 365; range: 1..36500)
#   Retention period for anonymous raw event rows.
#
# analytics_enhanced_retention_days (optional, default: 90; range: 1..36500)
#   Retention period for enhanced raw event rows.
#
# analytics_archive_retention_days (optional, default: 730; range: 1..36500)
#   Retention period for private archived aggregate cells.
#
# analytics_maintenance_batch_size (optional, default: 1000; range: 100..10000)
#   Maximum raw rows processed in each maintenance batch.
#
# When archiving and retention are both enabled, both raw retention periods
# must be at least analytics_archive_after_days. Whenever retention is enabled,
# archive retention must be at least the longer raw retention period. Schedule the maintenance command
# externally (normally daily): php bin/console app:analytics:maintain
# Uppercase environment variables with the same names override these values.
